            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial ischemia with aortocoronary artery gradient reversal during right coronary angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>186-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aortocoronary gradients are useful in assessing luminal obstructions and collateral supply during PTCA. Reversibility of collateral flow is demonstrated in a 51-year old angina patient.</AbstractText>
